WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.266 --> 00:00:17.796
The garden was not the only one that Dickon worked in.

2
00:00:18.997 --> 00:00:22.820
At his family's cottage on the moor was a garden surrounded by a low wall.

3
00:00:23.901 --> 00:00:26.543
Dickon grew all sorts of vegetables and flowers there.

4
00:00:27.664 --> 00:00:31.667
When he worked in the garden after supper, his mother liked to sit on the wall and talk

5
00:00:31.707 --> 00:00:31.988
to him.

6
00:00:33.472 --> 00:00:36.915
The children had agreed that Dickon's mother could know about the secret garden.

7
00:00:38.196 --> 00:00:43.800
So Dickon told her everything: from how Mary had found the key to what Ben had said when

8
00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:45.302
he discovered them in the garden.

9
00:00:45.322 --> 00:00:49.925
"It's a good thing that girl came to the manor," said Mother.

10
00:00:49.945 --> 00:00:53.969
"That's made her well and saved Colin.

11
00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:56.351
Standing on his feet!

12
00:00:57.592 --> 00:01:00.474
What does everyone at the manor think about his feeling so well?"

13
00:01:00.494 --> 00:01:02.896
"They don't know what to think."

14
00:01:04.724 --> 00:01:05.564
And that was true.

15
00:01:06.725 --> 00:01:09.566
The nurse was the first to notice that Colin was eating more.

16
00:01:09.586 --> 00:01:13.568
"You didn't used to eat," she said to him.

17
00:01:13.588 --> 00:01:16.689
"So many things bothered your stomach."

18
00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:21.371
"Nothing bothers my stomach these days," said Colin.

19
00:01:22.552 --> 00:01:27.674
The nurse gave him a strange look, and Colin realized he shouldn't appear too well just yet.

20
00:01:27.694 --> 00:01:31.956
"I mean, just a few things bother my stomach now."

21
00:01:33.216 --> 00:01:33.736
When Dr.

22
00:01:33.776 --> 00:01:36.497
Craven arrived, he asked a lot of questions.

23
00:01:36.517 --> 00:01:39.739
"You stay out in the gardens a great deal.

24
00:01:40.859 --> 00:01:41.439
Where do you go?"

25
00:01:41.459 --> 00:01:43.860
"I go to a place I like."

26
00:01:45.561 --> 00:01:48.062
"You seem to be gaining weight, and your color is better."

27
00:01:49.463 --> 00:01:50.603
"Perhaps I am feverish."

28
00:01:51.143 --> 00:01:52.744
Colin put on an air of gloom.

29
00:01:52.764 --> 00:01:56.986
"People who are not going to live are often different."

30
00:01:58.366 --> 00:01:59.747
Dr. Craven shook his head.

31
00:01:59.767 --> 00:02:02.068
"You're not feverish.

32
00:02:03.208 --> 00:02:07.252
If you keep getting better, we will have to tell your father of this remarkable improvement."

33
00:02:08.813 --> 00:02:11.515
But Colin wasn't ready to share the news with his father.

34
00:02:11.535 --> 00:02:13.837
"I won't have him told!"

35
00:02:14.277 --> 00:02:15.178
he said fiercely.

36
00:02:15.198 --> 00:02:18.601
"It will only disappoint him if I get worse again.

37
00:02:19.722 --> 00:02:22.324
You're making me angry, and I'm feeling worse already."

38
00:02:22.344 --> 00:02:24.366
"Hush, my boy.

39
00:02:25.487 --> 00:02:27.608
No letters will be written without your permission."

40
00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:33.309
Dr. Craven studied Colin with a puzzled look, and then he went on his way.

41
00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:37.473
Mary and Colin were quite alarmed after the doctor's visit.

42
00:02:37.493 --> 00:02:42.457
"I want to surprise my father by walking into his study," Colin told her.

43
00:02:42.477 --> 00:02:47.701
"We must pretend that you are much worse than you really are," said Mary.

44
00:02:49.342 --> 00:02:54.807
So starting that day, Colin made sure to complain when the footman carried him downstairs to his wheelchair.

45
00:02:56.128 --> 00:03:00.472
Mary made sympathetic noises and hovered over him as if he were terribly ill.

46
00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.120
There was only one problem.

47
00:03:04.441 --> 00:03:07.582
Mary and Colin were growing, and they were very hungry.

48
00:03:09.282 --> 00:03:14.164
They didn't dare ask for more food because the servants would realize Colin was getting better.

49
00:03:15.444 --> 00:03:19.465
One evening Dickon told his mother about this problem, and she had an idea.

50
00:03:19.485 --> 00:03:24.407
"When you go to see them in the morning, take a pail of new milk.

51
00:03:25.667 --> 00:03:28.168
I'll bake a crusty loaf of bread or some buns."

52
00:03:30.272 --> 00:03:33.694
The next day Dickon surprised Mary and Colin with the milk and buns.

53
00:03:33.714 --> 00:03:38.617
"There's magic in your mother, just as there is in you," said Colin.

54
00:03:38.637 --> 00:03:41.979
"It makes her think of ways to do nice things.

55
00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.820
Tell her we are grateful, Dickon."

56
00:03:46.341 --> 00:03:48.062
Dickon brought them food every day.

57
00:03:49.783 --> 00:03:52.445
After a while Mary and Colin remembered that Mrs.

58
00:03:52.525 --> 00:03:54.526
Sowerby had a large family to feed.

59
00:03:55.747 --> 00:03:57.528
So they began to pay her for their food.

60
00:03:58.824 --> 00:04:01.905
Then Dickon made a discovery in the woods outside the garden.

61
00:04:03.085 --> 00:04:07.527
There was a deep hole where he could build a tiny oven out of stones for roasting potatoes

62
00:04:07.687 --> 00:04:08.227
and eggs.

63
00:04:10.008 --> 00:04:11.568
Now they could really have a feast!

64
00:04:12.828 --> 00:04:16.069
Of course, when they went inside for lunch, they weren't hungry.

65
00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:18.630
"Look!" said Mrs.

66
00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:21.071
Medlock to the nurse as she carried away their dishes.

67
00:04:21.091 --> 00:04:23.832
"They've hardly touched their food.

68
00:04:25.108 --> 00:04:26.248
The cook is afraid Mr.

69
00:04:26.328 --> 00:04:29.489
Craven will blame her if they starve themselves to death."

70
00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:34.131
The nurse saved the tray of uneaten food to show Dr.

71
00:04:34.151 --> 00:04:38.292
Craven. He was very puzzled when he came to examine Colin.

72
00:04:39.452 --> 00:04:41.253
"I'm sorry to hear that you are not eating.

73
00:04:42.293 --> 00:04:43.293
This will not do.

74
00:04:44.233 --> 00:04:46.034
You will lose all the weight that you've gained."

75
00:04:46.054 --> 00:04:48.715
"I told you I wasn't well."

76
00:04:50.255 --> 00:04:53.576
Mary started to laugh, but quickly turned her giggle into a cough.

77
00:04:57.602 --> 00:05:00.784
Dr. Craven left the children together and went to talk to Mrs.

78
00:05:00.844 --> 00:05:05.849
Medlock. "Going without food seems to agree with them, so I guess we shouldn't worry.

79
00:05:07.010 --> 00:05:08.411
That boy is a new creature."

80
00:05:08.431 --> 00:05:11.794
"And so is that girl.

81
00:05:12.894 --> 00:05:14.836
Mary is even beginning to look pretty.

82
00:05:16.037 --> 00:05:20.421
She used to be so unhappy, but now she and Colin laugh together all the time.

83
00:05:21.682 --> 00:05:23.804
Maybe they're growing fat on laughter."

84
00:05:25.005 --> 00:05:28.359
"Then let them laugh," said Dr.

85
00:05:28.399 --> 00:05:28.801
Craven.
